//! Embedded columns in table DDL, on 3306 and 3307
//! ([`sprig_sql::embedcol`] parses and writes the statements):
//!
//! ```text
//! CREATE TABLE ... (c VECTOR(n) GENERATED BY EMBEDDING(src) USING MODEL 'm' ...)
//! ALTER TABLE t ADD [COLUMN] c VECTOR(n) GENERATED BY EMBEDDING(src) USING MODEL 'm' ...
//!   each clause: a name of at most 40 characters; ON CHANGE ASYNC (SYNC
//!   isn't built: 39997); the alias in ai.embedding_models, a local model
//!   (a provider's: 39997), n its dimensions (39997); the table has a
//!   primary key (39997)
//!   the statement with c VECTOR(n) NULL and the hidden _src and _hash
//!   columns, run through the session (its privileges apply) with the
//!   hidden names allowed; MariaDB checks the source as a generated
//!   column's
//!   then: an ai_embedded_columns row (generation 1, backfilling) and a
//!   feed subscription emb:e<id> at the feed's position now; the
//!   controller's ai_embed loop gives it a worker job that fills c
//! ALTER TABLE t MODIFY [COLUMN] c VECTOR(n) GENERATED BY EMBEDDING ...
//!   alone in its statement: a new model, source or token cap starts a
//!   re-embedding: shadow columns _sprig_emb_c_g<g+1> (and _src when the
//!   source changed), row pending, state reembedding; the worker fills
//!   them and renames them into place; the same declaration again changes
//!   nothing
//! ALTER TABLE t DROP [COLUMN] c: the hidden columns go too, then the row
//!   and the subscription
//! ALTER TABLE t CHANGE | MODIFY | RENAME COLUMN | ALTER COLUMN c: 39997
//! ```
//!
//! A statement that names a `_sprig_` column itself is never run with the
//! hidden names allowed: the name layer refuses it as usual.

